      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Properties of a Hyperbolic Paraboloid",
      "problem": "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z-5=5(x-1)^{2}-3(y+4)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-5 & =5(x-1)^{2}-3(y+4)^{2} \\\\ z-5 & =\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1/5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{1/3} \\\\ z-5 & =\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1/5}-\\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{1/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(1,-4,5).$",
